hadiths[158]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah destroy the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of prostration."
"4291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah destroy the Jews; when Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, forbade them fat, they melted it down, then sold it and consumed its price."
"4292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah destroy a people who make images of what they cannot create."
"4293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fight in defence of your wealth until you protect your wealth or are killed, and so become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter."
"4294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The killer of Ammar and the one who strips him of his belongings are in Hell."
"4295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fight them until they testify that la ilaha illallahu wa anna Muhammadan rasulullah (there is no true god except Allah, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah). When they do that, they have protected their lives and their wealth from you, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."
"4296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep to moderation and stay on the right course, for every hardship that befalls a Muslim is an expiation for his sins, even the stumble he suffers or the thorn that pricks him."
"4297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep to moderation, stay on the right course, and rejoice, and know that none of you will be saved by his deeds, not even I, unless Allah covers me with His mercy and grace."
"4298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two judges are in Hell and one judge is in Paradise: the judge who recognised the truth and judged according to it is in Paradise; and the judge who recognised the truth but deliberately acted unjustly, or who judged without knowledge, both of them are in Hell."
"4299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cuts down a lote tree, Allah will throw him headlong into Hell."
"4300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: When I test one of My believing servants and he praises Me and is patient with what I have tested him with, he rises from that bed of his as free of sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him. And the Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, says to the guardian angels: I have restrained this servant of Mine and tested him, so keep recording for him the same reward you used to record for him before this, when he was healthy."
"4301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: When I test My believing servant and he does not complain about Me to those who visit him in his illness, I release him from My captivity, then I give him flesh better than his flesh and blood better than his blood, and then he begins his deeds anew."
"4302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: When I afflict My servant in his two beloved things (meaning his eyes) and he then shows patience, I give him Paradise in exchange for them."
"4303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: When My servant loves to meet Me, I love to meet him, and when he dislikes meeting Me, I dislike meeting him."
"4304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: When the servant draws near to Me by a handspan, I draw near to him by a cubit; and when he draws near to Me by a cubit, I draw near to him by two cubits; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him running."
"4305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: When I take away My servant's two precious things, and he is patient over them and knows their worth, and praises Me for them, I am not pleased to give him any reward less than Paradise."
"4306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: When My servant intends to do a good deed but does not do it, I record it for him as one good deed; and if he does it, I record it for him as ten good deeds up to seven hundred times. And when he intends to do an evil deed but does not do it, I do not record it against him; and if he does it, I record it as only one evil deed."
"4307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never occurred to the heart of any human being."
"4308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Fasting is a shield by which the servant protects himself from the Fire. It is for Me, and I Myself will reward it."
"4309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Grandeur is My cloak, so whoever contends with Me over My cloak, I will break him."
"4310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Grandeur is My cloak and might is My lower garment, so whoever contends with Me over anything of them, I will punish him."
"4311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Pride is My cloak and majesty is My lower garment, so whoever contends with Me over either one of them, I will cast him into the Fire."
"4312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Those who love one another for the sake of My majesty (glory) will have pulpits of light, which even the prophets and the martyrs will envy."
"4313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I am the One most free of need of any partner. Whoever does a deed in which he associates someone else with Me, I abandon him and his association."
"4314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I created the rahm (kinship) and derived for it a name from My own name. So whoever joins it, I will join him (with My mercy); whoever severs it, I will sever him (from My mercy); and whoever cuts it off completely, I too will cut him off completely."
"4315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. If he thinks good, it is for him, and if he thinks ill, it is for him."
"4316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes."
"4317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Spend, and I will spend on you."
"4318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Indeed, the believer is, in My sight, worthy of every good. I draw out his soul from between his sides while he is praising Me."
"4319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: The people of your Ummah will keep on (asking questions): it is like this, it is like that, until they say: This is Allah, who created the creation, so who created Allah Almighty?"
"4320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: My love is due to those who love one another. I will shade them in the shade of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection, the day when there will be no shade but My shade."
"4321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: My love is due to those who love one another for My sake; My love is due to those who keep (ties) with one another for My sake; My love is due to those who sincerely advise one another for My sake; My love is due to those who visit one another for My sake; and My love is due to those who give (generously) to one another for My sake. Those who love one another for My sake will be on pulpits of light, and the prophets, the truthful ones and the martyrs will envy them for their position."
"4322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: My mercy has prevailed over My wrath."
"4323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: The son of Adam reviled Me, though it does not befit him to revile Me, and he denied Me, though it does not befit him to deny Me. As for his reviling Me, it is his saying that I have a child, whereas I am Allah, the One, the Self-Sufficient; I have not begotten, nor was I begotten, and there is none equal to Me. And as for his denying Me, it is his saying that Allah will not recreate me as He created me the first time, whereas creating the creation the first time is not harder for Me than recreating it."
"4324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O My servant! When you remember Me in solitude, I remember you in solitude; and if you remember Me in a gathering, I remember you in a gathering better and greater than it."
"4325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O My servant! I am as you think of Me, and I am with you when you remember Me."
"4326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I have divided the prayer (Surah al-Fatihah) between Myself and My servant into two halves, and My servant shall have what he asks. When the servant says: 'All praise is for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds,' Allah says: My servant has praised Me. When he says: 'The Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate,' Allah says: My servant has extolled Me. When he says: 'Master of the Day of Judgement,' Allah says: My servant has glorified Me. When he says: 'You alone we worship and You alone we ask for help,' Allah says: This (verse) is between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks. And when he says: 'Guide us to the straight path, the path of those You have blessed, not of those who have incurred wrath, nor of those who are astray,' Allah says: This is for My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks."
"4327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: The son of Adam denied Me, though he should not have done so, and he reviled Me, though he should not have done so. As for his denying Me, he claimed that I am not able to recreate him as he was before; and as for his reviling Me, he said that I have a child, whereas I am far above taking a wife or a child."
"4328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Every deed of the son of Adam is for himself except fasting; it is for Me, and I Myself will reward it. Fasting is a shield. So when it is the day of fasting for any of you, let him not speak obscenely nor raise his voice in clamour, and if someone reviles him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! The smell of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasing to Allah than the fragrance of musk. And the fasting person has two joys in which he rejoices: when he breaks his fast, he rejoices at breaking it, and when he meets his Lord, he will rejoice at his fasting."
"4329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says to the soul: Come out! And it says: I will not come out except unwillingly."
"4330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Whoever knows that I have the power to forgive sins, I forgive him and I do not mind, as long as he does not associate anything with Me."
"4331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: My love is due to those who love one another for My sake, sit together for My sake, give (generously) to one another for My sake, and visit one another for My sake."
"4332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: By My might and My majesty! I will not combine for My servant two securities or two fears. If he feels secure from Me in this world, I will make him afraid on the day I gather My servants; and if he fears Me in this world, I will grant him security on the day I gather My servants."
"4333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Who is more unjust than one who sets out to create a creation like My creation? Let them create a grain, or let them create a speck, or let them at least create a grain of barley."
"4334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: The vow does not bring the son of Adam anything that I had not already decreed; rather, the vow leads him to the decree that I had already written for him. Through it I extract (wealth) from the miser, so he gives Me for it what he would not give Me before."
"4335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: No servant remembers Me in himself but that I remember him in a gathering of My angels, and he does not remember Me in a gathering but that I remember him in the Highest Company (the most exalted assembly of angels)."
"4336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: It is not proper for any servant of Mine to say: I am better than Yunus bin Matta."
"4337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! If you remember Me in yourself, I will remember you in Myself; if you remember Me in a gathering, I will remember you in a gathering better than it; if you draw near to Me by a handspan, I will draw near to you by a cubit; if you draw near to Me by a cubit, I will draw near to you by a ba' (the length of both arms outstretched); and if you come to Me walking, I will come to you running."
"4338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! As long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I will keep forgiving you, whatever you have done, and I do not mind. O son of Adam! Even if your sins were to reach the edges of the sky and you then sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you, and I do not mind. O son of Adam! If you were to come to Me with sins filling the earth, and then meet Me without having associated anything with Me, I would come to you with as much forgiveness."
"4339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! Pray four rak'ahs for Me at the start of the day, and I will suffice you for the latter part of it."
"4340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! Stand up towards Me, and I will come walking towards you; and walk towards Me, and I will come running towards you."
"4341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! As long as you worship Me, hope in Me and do not associate anything with Me, I will keep forgiving you, whatever you have done. And if you face Me with errors and sins filling the heavens and the earth, I will face you with as much forgiveness, and I will forgive you, and I do not mind."
"4342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! Do not be lazy in praying four rak'ahs at the start of the day, and I will suffice you for the latter part of it."
"4343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: The son of Adam hurts Me; he reviles time, whereas I am time. The whole matter is in My Hand; it is I who alternate the night and the day."
"4344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: 'The son of Adam hurts Me; he says: Alas, the misfortune of time! So let none of you say: Alas, the misfortune of time! For I am Time; I alternate its night and its day, and whenever I wish, I bring them to an end.'"
"4345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: 'O My servants! I have made oppression forbidden for Myself and I have made it forbidden among you as well, so do not oppress one another. O My servants! All of you are astray except the one whom I guide, so seek guidance from Me and I will guide you. O My servants! All of you are hungry except the one whom I feed, so ask Me for food and I will feed you. O My servants! All of you are naked except the one whom I clothe, so ask Me for clothing and I will clothe you. O My servants! You sin by night and by day, and I forgive all sins, so seek forgiveness from Me and I will forgive you. O My servants! You will never have the power to harm Me so as to harm Me, nor the power to benefit Me so as to benefit Me. O My servants! If the first of you and the last of you, and your humans and your jinn, were all to become like the most God-fearing heart of a single man among you, that would add nothing to My dominion. O My servants! If the first of you and the last of you, and your humans and your jinn, were all to become like the most wicked heart of a single man among you, that would take nothing away from My dominion. O My servants! If the first of you and the last of you, and your humans and your jinn, were all to stand on a single plain and ask of Me, and I were to give every person what he asked for, that would decrease My treasure only as much as a needle decreases the sea when it is dipped into it. O My servants! It is only your deeds, which I record for you, then I will repay you for them in full. So whoever finds good, let him praise Allah, and whoever finds something other than that, let him blame no one but himself.'"
"4346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man said: 'I will certainly give charity tonight.' So he went out with his charity and (unknowingly) placed it in the hand of a thief. In the morning people began talking: 'Charity was given to a thief last night.' He said: 'O Allah, all praise is Yours, (my charity went) to a thief! I will certainly give charity again tonight.' So he went out with his charity and placed it in the hand of an adulteress. In the morning people began talking: 'Charity was given to an adulteress last night.' He said: 'O Allah, all praise is Yours, (my charity went) to an adulteress! I will certainly give charity again tonight.' So he went out with his charity and placed it in the hand of a wealthy man. In the morning people began talking: 'Charity was given to a wealthy man last night.' He said: 'O Allah, all praise is Yours, (my charity went) to a thief, to an adulteress and to a wealthy man!' Then (an angel) came to him and he was told: 'As for your charity to the thief, perhaps he will refrain from his stealing; as for the adulteress, perhaps she will refrain from her adultery; and as for the wealthy man, perhaps he will take a lesson and spend from what Allah has given him.'"
"4347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man said: 'Allah will never forgive so-and-so!' So Allah Almighty revealed to one of the prophets: 'This (speaker) has become a sinner, so let him begin his deeds anew.'"
"4348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sulayman bin Dawud (peace be upon him) said: 'Tonight I will certainly go round to a hundred of my wives, and each of them will give birth to a horseman who will fight in the path of Allah.' His companion said to him: 'Say: In sha' Allah (if Allah wills).' But he did not say: In sha' Allah. So he went to all of them, and none of them conceived except one woman, who gave birth to half a human being. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! Had he said: In sha' Allah, his oath would not have been broken, and it would have been the means of attaining his wish."
"4349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) said to me: 'We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or pictures.'"
"4350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) said to me: 'Give Khadijah the glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of pearl, in which there is neither clamour nor toil.'"
"4351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) said to me: 'Take Hafsah back, for she fasts much and stands much in prayer at night, and she will be your wife in Paradise as well.'"
"4352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) said to me: 'Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak,' so I recited it. Then he said: 'Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind,' so I recited it too."
"4353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) said to me: 'If only you had seen me as I was taking the mud (silt) of the sea and stuffing it into the mouth of Pharaoh, for fear that mercy might reach him.'"
"4354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) said to me: 'Whoever of your Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.' I asked: 'Even if he committed adultery and even if he stole?' He said: 'Even if he committed adultery and even if he stole.'"
"4355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) said to me: 'O Muhammad! Live as long as you wish, for you must die in any case; love whomever you wish, for you must part from him in any case; and do whatever you wish, for you must meet it in any case.'"
"4356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels said: 'O Lord! This servant of Yours wants to commit an evil deed, while You see him well.' Allah Almighty said: 'Watch him. If he commits it, write it down for him as one evil deed like it; and if he leaves it, write it down for him as a good deed, for he left it only for My sake.'"
"4357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Musa (peace be upon him) stood up to deliver a sermon among the Children of Israel, and he was asked: 'Who is the most knowledgeable of people?' He said: 'I am.' So Allah Almighty reproached him because he did not attribute knowledge to Allah, and Allah Almighty revealed to him: 'I have a servant at the junction of the two seas who is more knowledgeable than you.' Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'O Lord! How can I reach him?' He was told: 'Take a fish in a basket; when you find it missing, that is the place.' So he set out, and his attendant Yusha' bin Nun set out with him, the two of them carrying a fish in a basket, until they reached a rock, laid down their heads and fell asleep. The fish slipped out of the basket and made its way into the sea like a tunnel. This was a cause of wonder for Musa (peace be upon him) and his attendant. They travelled on for the rest of their day and night, and when morning came, Musa (peace be upon him) said to his attendant: 'Bring us our morning meal; we have certainly met with great fatigue on this journey of ours.' Musa (peace be upon him) had not felt any fatigue until he had passed beyond the place that Allah had commanded him to reach. His attendant said: 'Did you see, when we took shelter at the rock? I forgot the fish.' Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'That is exactly what we were seeking.' So the two of them returned, retracing their footsteps. When they reached the rock, they saw a man lying covered with a garment. Musa (peace be upon him) greeted him with salam, and Khidr (peace be upon him) said: 'Where does salam come from in this land of yours?' Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'I am Musa.' He asked: 'Musa of the Children of Israel?' He said: 'Yes.' Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'May I follow you so that you teach me some of the right guidance that you have been taught?' Khidr (peace be upon him) said: 'You will not be able to have patience with me. O Musa! I have a knowledge from the knowledge of Allah which Allah has taught me and which you do not know, and you have a knowledge from the knowledge of Allah which Allah has taught you and which I do not know.' Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'You will find me patient, if Allah wills, and I will not disobey you in any matter.' So the two of them set off walking along the shore. A boat passed by, and they asked the people of the boat to take them on board. The people of the boat recognised Khidr (peace be upon him) and took them on board without any fare. Then a sparrow came, alighted on the edge of the boat and pecked once or twice in the sea. Khidr (peace be upon him) said: 'O Musa! My knowledge and your knowledge have diminished the knowledge of Allah no more than the pecking of this sparrow has diminished this sea.' Then Khidr (peace be upon him) went to one of the planks of the boat and pulled it out. Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'These people carried us without a fare, and you have made a hole in their boat to drown its passengers?' Khidr (peace be upon him) said: 'Did I not say that you would not be able to have patience with me?' Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'Do not take me to task for what I forgot.' So the first (objection) from Musa (peace be upon him) was out of forgetfulness. Then the two of them set off until (they came upon) a boy playing with other boys, and Khidr (peace be upon him) seized his head and pulled it off with his hand. Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'Have you killed an innocent soul, not in retaliation for a soul?' Khidr (peace be upon him) said: 'Did I not tell you that you would not be able to have patience with me?' Then the two of them went on until they came to the people of a town and asked them for food, but they refused to host them. There they found a wall that was about to collapse, and Khidr (peace be upon him) set it upright with his hand. Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'If you had wished, you could have taken a wage for it.' Khidr (peace be upon him) said: 'This is the parting between me and you.' May Allah have mercy on Musa; we wished that he had been patient, so that he would have told us more of their story."
"4358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim's fighting his (Muslim) brother is disbelief, and abusing him is sinfulness."
"4359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fighting a Muslim is disbelief and abusing him is sinfulness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to cut off his (Muslim) brother for more than three days."
"4360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who is bound and then (unjustly) killed, this killing of his leaves no sin without wiping it out."
"4361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The killing of a believer is greater (graver) in the sight of Allah than the passing away of the world."
"4362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They killed him, may Allah destroy them! Why did they not ask when they did not know? The cure for ignorance is only to ask. It would have been enough for him to perform tayammum."
"4363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They killed him, may Allah destroy them! Was not the cure for ignorance to ask?"
"4364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has rewarded you and has returned (your share) to you through the inheritance."
"4365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two Eids have come together on this day of yours, so whoever wishes, this (Eid prayer) suffices him in place of the Jumu'ah; and we, if Allah wills, will hold the Jumu'ah."
"4366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Hani! We have granted protection to the one to whom you granted protection."
"4367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has given you permission to go out for your needs."
"4368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, successful is the one who embraced Islam, was given provision sufficient for his needs, and whom Allah made content with what He gave him."
"4369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am leaving you upon a bright and clear path (of the religion), whose night is as bright as its day; after me no one will deviate from it except one who is doomed to destruction. Whoever of you lives will soon see much disagreement, so it is binding upon you to hold firmly to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the guided Rightly-Guided Caliphs, which you know; bite onto it with your molars. And obedience is binding upon you, even if (your ruler) is an Abyssinian slave, for the believer is like the camel with a nose-rein: wherever it is led, it goes."
"4370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you gave birth to your child, you became free (from your waiting period)."
"4371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise was brought so near to me that, had I dared to reach for it, I would have brought you a cluster from its fruits; and Hell was brought so near to me that I said: 'O Lord, am I with them too?' Then (suddenly) I saw a woman being clawed by a cat. I asked: 'What is her case?' It was said: 'She kept it (the cat) confined until it died of hunger; she neither fed it nor let it go so that it could eat the vermin of the earth.'"
"4372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Just now, since I led you in prayer, I saw Paradise and Hell presented before me in the direction of this wall; I have never seen the like of this day in good and evil."
"4373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has had mercy on her because of her compassion for her two sons."
"4374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have asked Allah for something concerning appointed life spans, numbered days and apportioned provisions; none of them will come sooner than its time, nor will any of them be delayed beyond its time. Had you asked Allah to protect you from the punishment of the Fire and the punishment of the grave, that would have been better and more excellent for you."
"4375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty was greatly pleased (He marvelled) at how the two of you treated your guest tonight."
"4376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We have completed the prayer, so whoever wishes to sit for the sermon may sit, and whoever wishes to leave may leave."
"4377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the nations that passed before you there were people who were spoken to (by the angels) (muhaddath); if there is any such person in my Ummah, it is Umar bin al-Khattab."
"4378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I used to dislike that you should say: 'Whatever Allah and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) will'; rather say: 'Whatever Allah wills, then what Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) wills.'"
"4379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from visiting graves, but now Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has been given permission to visit his mother's grave, so do visit graves, for they remind you of the Hereafter."
"4380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty wrote the destinies fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earths."
"4381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When I came to Madinah, the people of Madinah had two days on which they used to play during the time of Ignorance. (So I said:) Allah Almighty has given you in their place two days better than them: the day of Eid al-Fitr and the day of Eid al-Adha (sacrifice)."
"4382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Put Quraysh in front and do not go ahead of them; learn from Quraysh and do not teach them. Were it not that I fear Quraysh would become arrogant, I would tell them what rank the best of them have in the sight of Allah Almighty."
"4383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Put Quraysh in front and do not go ahead of them; learn from them and do not teach them."
"4384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Put Quraysh in front and do not go ahead of them. Were it not that I fear Quraysh would become arrogant, I would tell them what rank they have in the sight of Allah."
"4385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Lead him by his hand."
"4386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Bring it near (serve it), for it has reached its proper place (its due time)."
"4387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Bring it near (eat it), for a house in which there is vinegar is not lacking in condiment."
"4388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An ant bit one of the prophets, so he ordered that the whole colony of ants be burned. Thereupon Allah Almighty revealed to him: 'Because one ant bit you, you have burned a whole nation that glorified (Allah)?!'"
"4389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Quraysh, the Ansar, Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, Ashja' and Ghifar (all of these) are my allies; they have no patron other than Allah and His Messenger."
"4390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Quraysh will be the rulers of the people, in both good and evil, until the Day of Resurrection."
"4391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Quraysh are the rightful holders of this matter (the caliphate), so the righteous among the people follow their righteous, and the wicked among the people follow their wicked."
"4392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trim the moustaches and let the beards grow."
"4393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Returning (from the journey) is also equal to a military expedition."
"4394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stay at these sacred sites of yours (the places of Hajj), for you are upon one of the inheritances of your father Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"4395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: I believe in Allah, then remain steadfast upon it."
"4396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak' and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind' - people have not sought refuge with anything better than these two."
"4397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: As-salamu alaykum (peace be upon you), may I come in?"
"4398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, grant me well-being and provide for me, for these (supplications) gather for you both your world and your Hereafter."
"4399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my hearing, from the evil of my sight, from the evil of my tongue, from the evil of my heart and from the evil of my semen (desire)."
"4400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself greatly, and none forgives sins except You, so grant me forgiveness from Yourself and have mercy on me; indeed You are the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful."
"4401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, guide me and keep me on the right course. And by guidance, call to mind your being guided along the path, and by the right course, the straight aim of an arrow."
"4402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Lord of everything and its Sovereign! I bear witness that there is no true god except You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self and from the evil of Satan and his polytheism. Recite this (supplication) in the morning, in the evening and when you lie down in your bed."
"4403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say just as they (the callers to prayer) say, then when you have finished, ask and you will be given."
"4404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Say: He is Allah, the One' (Surah al-Ikhlas) is equal to one third of the Qur'an."
"4405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Say: He is Allah, the One' is equal to one third of the Qur'an, and 'Say: O disbelievers!' is equal to one quarter of the Qur'an."
"4406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite Surah al-Ikhlas and the Mu'awwidhatayn (Surah al-Falaq and Surah al-Nas) three times each in the evening and the morning; they will suffice you against everything."
"4407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The heart of an old man remains young in the love of two things: love of life and love of wealth."
"4408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The heart of an old man remains young in the love of two things: a long life and abundant wealth."
"4409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A grateful heart, a tongue that remembers (Allah), and a righteous wife who helps you in the affairs of your religion and your world - this is the best treasure that people can amass."
"4410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever intoxicates in a large quantity, even a small quantity of it is unlawful."
"4411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I stood at the gate of Paradise and saw that most of those who entered it were the poor (the needy), while the wealthy were held back - except for the people of the Fire, for they had already been ordered to the Fire. And I stood at the gate of the Fire and saw that most of those who entered it were women."
"4412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The legs of my pulpit are firmly set in Paradise."
"4413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The survival of my Ummah is (also) by means of its worst people."
"4414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, send Your mercy upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), the unlettered Prophet, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your mercy upon the family of Ibrahim; and send Your blessings upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), the unlettered Prophet, as You sent Your blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the worlds; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And as for the salam, it is just as you already know."
"4415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, send Your mercy upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), who is Your servant and Messenger, as You sent Your mercy upon Ibrahim; and send Your blessings upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim."
"4416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, send Your mercy upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your mercy upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, send Your blessings upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"4417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, send Your mercy upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), his wives and his offspring, as You sent Your mercy upon Ibrahim; and send Your blessings upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), his wives and his offspring, as You sent Your blessings upon Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"4418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep moderation in your speech (do not go to excess), and do not let Satan gain mastery over you."
"4419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Speak good and you will gain (reward), and keep silent from evil and you will remain safe."
"4420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say it like this: What Allah wills, and then what you will."
"4421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: Peace be upon you, O believers and Muslims, dwellers of these abodes (the graves)! May Allah have mercy on those of us who have gone ahead and those who come later, and indeed we, if Allah wills, shall be joining you."
"4422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, forgive me and him, and after him grant me a good recompense."
"4423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, You are indeed the One who pardons, You love to pardon, so pardon me."
"4424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens, Lord of the Mighty Throne, our Lord and the Lord of everything! Revealer of the Torah, the Injil and the Qur'an, the One who splits the seed and the date-stone to make them grow! I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock is in Your hand. You are the First, there is nothing before You; You are the Last, there is nothing after You; You are the Manifest, there is nothing above You; and You are the Hidden, there is nothing nearer than You. Pay off my debt for me and free me from need of poverty."
"4425","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am, and my place (of leaving ihram) on the earth shall be wherever You hold me back. For if you have made this condition, then you are owed by your Lord whatever exception you have made."
"4426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rise up towards a Paradise whose width is that of the heavens and the earth."
"4427","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stand up to receive your chief."
"4428","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stand up, for death has an alarm (a state of dread) to it."
"4429","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Standing for one hour in the rank for fighting in the path of Allah is better than sixty years of standing (in worship)."
"4430","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Children of Israel were told: 'Enter the gate prostrating and say: Hittah (forgive our sins)', but they changed (the command) and entered crawling on their buttocks, and said: A grain within a barley corn."
"4431","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take a midday nap (qaylulah, a short rest at noon), for the devils do not take a midday nap."
"4432","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tie (the camel), and then put your trust in Allah."
"4433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tie it, and then put your trust in Allah."
"4434","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Preserve knowledge by writing it down."
"4435","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who takes charge (of the caliphate) after me is in Paradise, and the one who takes charge after him is in Paradise, and the third and the fourth are also in Paradise."
"4436","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The killer does not inherit (from the one he killed)."
"4437","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who sits (waiting) for the prayer is like one who is devoutly obedient, and a man is counted among those praying from the time he leaves his house until he returns to his house."
"4438","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, (dying of) the plague is martyrdom, (dying of) a disease of the belly is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and dying in the state of postnatal bleeding is martyrdom."
"4439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, (dying of) the plague is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, (dying of) a disease of the belly is martyrdom, burning to death is martyrdom, and (dying of) tuberculosis (is martyrdom), and as for the woman who dies in the state of postnatal bleeding, her child will pull her by its umbilical cord into Paradise."
"4440","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Being killed in the path of Allah expiates every sin except debt."
"4441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one who dies of a disease of the belly is a martyr, the one who dies of the plague is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, and the woman who dies in the state of postnatal bleeding is a martyr."
"4442","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qadariyyah (those who deny divine decree) are the Magians of this Ummah. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend their funerals."
"4443","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an is an intercessor whose intercession will be accepted, and an advocate who disputes and whose word will be believed. Whoever puts it in front of him, it will lead him to Paradise, and whoever throws it behind him, it will drive him to Hell."
"4444","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an may be recited according to seven ahruf (modes of recitation), so do not dispute about the Qur'an, for disputing about the Qur'an is disbelief."
"4445","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Storytellers (preachers) are of three kinds: a ruler, one commanded (by a ruler), or one who is vain and self-conceited."
"4446","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Judges are of three kinds: two of them are in Hell and one is in Paradise. A man who knew the truth and judged according to it, he is in Paradise; a man who judged between people in ignorance, he is in Hell; and a man who recognised the truth but was unjust in his judgement, he is in Hell."
"4447","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Judges are of three kinds: two are in Hell and one is in Paradise. The judge who judged according to his desires is in Hell, the one who judged without knowledge is in Hell, and the one who judged according to the truth is in Paradise."
